Seam: chrome::CreateRestoredTab and chrome::AddRestoredTabImpl in
      chrome/browser/ui/browser_tabrestore.cc.
Why: session restore gives a tab a fresh SessionID, so Arcium cannot key a
     pinned entry on it. Chromium's per-tab session extra_data does survive a
     restart and reaches this file; two upstream features already consume it
     in CreateRestoredTab, one line each. Without this hook every pinned entry
     comes back cold and opens a second copy of its page when clicked.

     Two calls, not one, because the restore is in two halves. In
     CreateRestoredTab the WebContents is still a unique_ptr with no place in
     any tab strip, so there is no tabs::TabInterface and no tabs::TabHandle
     to bind; that is precisely why the two upstream neighbours there store
     their state on the WebContents. Arcium parks the id there too, and binds
     in AddRestoredTabImpl, right after the existing from_session_restore
     block, which has already resolved the tab from the contents.
Delegates to: arcium::StashRestoredEntryId, arcium::BindStashedEntryId.

